# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Privacy boundary — this repo is the public extraction of a private vault app.
#
# The paths below exist in the private source repo and MUST NOT be published.
# They are listed here rather than merely left unstaged so that a careless
# `git add -A` cannot publish them: the ignore rule is the guard, not discipline.
#
# `src/data/generated/` is the one deliberate exception to that pattern. It IS
# tracked here, but every file in it is a synthetic demo fixture — invented
# content in the real schema — because `src/data/vaultApi.js` imports them
# statically, so a clone with no fixtures cannot build. This is safe precisely
# because the sync script that would regenerate them from a real vault is not
# shipped (see ARCHITECTURE.md). Never overwrite them with synced output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
branding/
memory-bank/
scripts/
skills/
CLAUDE.md
USER.md
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real vault data — the ONLY place it may live in this repo, and it never
# enters git. src/data/vaultApi.js prefers these files at runtime and falls
# back to the tracked synthetic fixtures in src/data/generated/ when absent,
# so a fresh clone still builds and runs. Written by scripts/sync-vault-data.mjs.
#
# Do not "fix" a missing dashboard by copying real data into src/data/generated/
# — that path is tracked, and that is exactly how real tasks got published once.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/data/local/
